(1. Introduction and Project Objectives) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(SYNTHETIC TEST DATA. This report was generated to test ResearchPilot. Harbor Point) Tj
T*
(Community College, its staff, and every figure below are fictional and must not be cited) Tj
T*
(as real research.) Tj
T*
(The Harbor Point Community College Energy Storage Pilot added a battery energy storage) Tj
T*
(system to the campus microgrid in January 2025. The microgrid already had an 800 kW) Tj
T*
(rooftop solar array serving the Science Building and the Library. Without storage, most) Tj
T*
(of the midday solar output was exported to the grid at a low price, while electricity) Tj
T*
(was bought back at a high price during the evening peak.) Tj
T*
(The pilot had three objectives:) Tj
T*
(Objective 1: Store midday solar energy and use it during the evening peak, reducing grid) Tj
T*
(purchases.) Tj
T*
(Objective 2: Keep the Library's emergency lighting and network equipment running for at) Tj
T*
(least four hours during a grid outage.) Tj
T*
(Objective 3: Measure the real efficiency, capacity, safety, and costs of the system, to) Tj
T*
(decide whether to install storage at the college's second campus.) Tj
T*
(The pilot ran for twelve months, from January to December 2025. Section 2 compares the) Tj
T*
(battery options that were considered, Section 3 reports measured efficiency and) Tj
T*
(capacity, Section 4 covers safety and cost, and Section 5 lists the limitations of this) Tj
T*
(report.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
