(3. Efficiency and Capacity Results) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Measured results for the selected LFP system \(Option A\) over the twelve-month pilot:) Tj
T*
(Round-trip efficiency: the average measured round-trip efficiency was 90.5%, slightly) Tj
T*
(below the rated 92%. Most of the difference came from inverter losses and the energy) Tj
T*
(used by the cooling system.) Tj
T*
(Energy throughput: the battery charged 361 MWh of midday solar energy and discharged 327) Tj
T*
(MWh during the evening peak \(327 / 361 = 90.5%\). This corresponds to 330 full equivalent) Tj
T*
(cycles, an average of 0.9 cycles per day.) Tj
T*
(Capacity: the usable capacity was 1,000 kWh at the start of the pilot and 982 kWh after) Tj
T*
(twelve months, a capacity fade of 1.8% in the first year.) Tj
T*
(Power: the maximum discharge power is 250 kW, so a full discharge takes about four) Tj
T*
(hours.) Tj
T*
(Outage performance: during the only grid outage of the year, on 14 October 2025, lasting) Tj
T*
(2 hours and 30 minutes, the battery kept the Library's emergency lighting and network) Tj
T*
(equipment running without interruption, as required by Objective 2.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
