(4. Safety and Cost Considerations) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Safety: lithium iron phosphate cells have higher thermal stability than nickel manganese) Tj
T*
(cobalt cells, which was the main reason for choosing Option A over Option B. The battery) Tj
T*
(is housed in a separate container placed 3 metres from the Library, with gas detection) Tj
T*
(and a clean-agent fire suppression system. Two minor alarms occurred during the pilot: a) Tj
T*
(cooling-fan fault in March and a door-sensor fault in August. Neither involved) Tj
T*
(overheating, and there were no safety incidents.) Tj
T*
(Cost: Table 2 shows the installed cost of the system.) Tj
T*
(Table 2. Installed cost \(synthetic test data\)) Tj
T*
/F3 9 Tf
(Cost item                                   USD) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
/F3 9 Tf
(Battery modules \(1,000 kWh x USD 420/kWh\)   420,000) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
/F3 9 Tf
(Installation, inverter, grid integration    100,000) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
/F3 9 Tf
(Total installed cost                        520,000) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
(The measured savings in 2025 were USD 61,000, from lower evening electricity purchases) Tj
T*
(and lower peak-demand charges. The simple payback period is therefore about 8.5 years) Tj
T*
(\(520,000 / 61,000\). These figures do not include the annual maintenance contract \(see) Tj
T*
(Section 5\).) Tj
T*
ET
